{
  "trace_id": "7a7a68f1-02df-4012-9756-ef84aa5499e0",
  "model": "Qwen/Qwen3.5-35B-A3B",
  "question_id": "D1_002",
  "domain": "ethical_dilemmas",
  "run": 1,
  "nodes": [
    {
      "tu_id": 0,
      "text": "This is a profound ethical dilemma that highlights the critical boundary between **medical triage** and **social valuation**. In almost all established bioethical frameworks and AI governance guidelines, an AI system should **not** make this decision based on age, family status, or perceived social worth.",
      "start_char": 0,
      "end_char": 306,
      "token_count": 44,
      "boundary_class": "NONE",
      "node_type": "CMP",
      "node_family": "EVALUATION",
      "classification_confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
      "tu_id": 1,
      "text": "Here is how an ethical AI healthcare system should approach this scenario:",
      "start_char": 308,
      "end_char": 382,
      "token_count": 12,
      "boundary_class": "NONE",
      "node_type": "CMP",
      "node_family": "EVALUATION",
      "classification_confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
      "tu_id": 2,
      "text": "Adhere to Medical Criteria First: The primary metric for allocation must be medical necessity and likelihood of benefit.",
      "start_char": 384,
      "end_char": 510,
      "token_count": 18,
      "boundary_class": "BRANCH",
      "node_type": "RFR",
      "node_family": "EXPLORATION",
      "classification_confidence": 1.0
    },
    {
      "tu_id": 3,
      "text": "**The Scenario:** Since both patients have an **equal chance of survival**, the medical criteria are tied. **The Constraint:** Once medical criteria are exhausted, the system cannot pivot to subjective social judgments (e.g., \"the parent has more dependents\" or \"the teacher has lived a full life\").",
      "start_char": 511,
      "end_char": 814,
      "token_count": 45,
      "boundary_class": "NONE",
      "node_type": "SPC",
      "node_family": "ELABORATION",
      "classification_confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
      "tu_id": 4,
      "text": "Avoid \"Social Worth\" Judgments: Deciding based on age or family status introduces significant ethical risks:",
      "start_char": 820,
      "end_char": 934,
      "token_count": 15,
      "boundary_class": "BRANCH",
      "node_type": "RFR",
      "node_family": "EXPLORATION",
      "classification_confidence": 1.0
    },
    {
      "tu_id": 5,
      "text": "**Ageism:** Devaluing a life based on age (saving the 35-year-old over the 75-year-old) discriminates against the elderly. **Social Utility:** Valuing one life over another based on their role to society (a parent vs. a retired teacher) is considered ethically precarious. It implies some lives are more \"valuable\" than others, which violates the principle of human dignity.",
      "start_char": 935,
      "end_char": 1313,
      "token_count": 56,
      "boundary_class": "NONE",
      "node_type": "JUS",
      "node_family": "ELABORATION",
      "classification_confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
      "tu_id": 6,
      "text": "**Bias Amplification:** AI models trained on historical data often inherit biases. An algorithm deciding based on \"family status\" could inadvertently discriminate against single parents, childless individuals, or those without social support networks.",
      "start_char": 1318,
      "end_char": 1569,
      "token_count": 32,
      "boundary_class": "NONE",
      "node_type": "RFR",
      "node_family": "EXPLORATION",
      "classification_confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
      "tu_id": 7,
      "text": "Implement Neutral Allocation Protocols: If medical prognosis is identical, most international health guidelines (such as those from the WHO or crisis standards of care during pandemics) recommend one of the following neutral methods:",
      "start_char": 1575,
      "end_char": 1814,
      "token_count": 33,
      "boundary_class": "BRANCH",
      "node_type": "RFR",
      "node_family": "EXPLORATION",
      "classification_confidence": 1.0
    },
    {
      "tu_id": 8,
      "text": "**Randomization (Lottery):** A coin flip or computer-generated random selection. This ensures fairness and procedural justice, acknowledging that both patients have an equal right to the resource.",
      "start_char": 1815,
      "end_char": 2011,
      "token_count": 26,
      "boundary_class": "NONE",
      "node_type": "SPC",
      "node_family": "ELABORATION",
      "classification_confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
      "tu_id": 9,
      "text": "**First-Come-First-Served:** Allocation based on the order of admission or triage registration. This is administratively simple and avoids subjective scoring.",
      "start_char": 2016,
      "end_char": 2174,
      "token_count": 19,
      "boundary_class": "NONE",
      "node_type": "SPC",
      "node_family": "ELABORATION",
      "classification_confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
      "tu_id": 10,
      "text": "**Time to Benefit:** If there is any slight difference in the timeline of treatment required, that could be a neutral medical factor, but in this specific prompt, they are equal.",
      "start_char": 2179,
      "end_char": 2357,
      "token_count": 30,
      "boundary_class": "NONE",
      "node_type": "RFR",
      "node_family": "EXPLORATION",
      "classification_confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
      "tu_id": 11,
      "text": "Human-in-the-Loop Oversight: An AI should not be the sole decision-maker in life-or-death scenarios involving scarcity.",
      "start_char": 2363,
      "end_char": 2488,
      "token_count": 15,
      "boundary_class": "BRANCH",
      "node_type": "RFR",
      "node_family": "EXPLORATION",
      "classification_confidence": 1.0
    },
    {
      "tu_id": 12,
      "text": "**The AI's Role:** The AI should flag the case as a \"tie\" according to medical protocols and present the options to a human triage team. **The Human Role:** A multidisciplinary committee (doctors, ethicists, hospital administrators) should review the case. This ensures accountability and allows for the application of context-specific institutional policies.",
      "start_char": 2489,
      "end_char": 2852,
      "token_count": 51,
      "boundary_class": "NONE",
      "node_type": "MET",
      "node_family": "EVALUATION",
      "classification_confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
      "tu_id": 13,
      "text": "Transparency and Policy: The rules governing the AI must be transparent and publicly agreed upon *before* the crisis occurs.",
      "start_char": 2858,
      "end_char": 2988,
      "token_count": 19,
      "boundary_class": "BRANCH",
      "node_type": "RFR",
      "node_family": "EXPLORATION",
      "classification_confidence": 1.0
    },
    {
      "tu_id": 14,
      "text": "**Pre-defined Policy:** The hospital or health system should have published guidelines stating how ties are broken (e.g., \"If medical prognosis is equal, a lottery will be used\"). **Auditability:** The AI must log why a decision was made (or why it deferred to humans) to ensure it was not acting on hidden biases.",
      "start_char": 2989,
      "end_char": 3307,
      "token_count": 52,
      "boundary_class": "CONVERGENCE",
      "node_type": "SYN",
      "node_family": "CONVERGENCE",
      "classification_confidence": 1.0
    },
    {
      "tu_id": 15,
      "text": "Conclusion: **The AI should not choose between them based on their ages or family situations.**",
      "start_char": 3313,
      "end_char": 3411,
      "token_count": 15,
      "boundary_class": "BRANCH",
      "node_type": "SYN",
      "node_family": "CONVERGENCE",
      "classification_confidence": 1.0
    },
    {
      "tu_id": 16,
      "text": "The most ethically defensible path is for the AI to **flag the case as a medical tie** and recommend a **randomized selection (lottery)** or defer to a **human ethics committee** to apply the institution's pre-established, neutral allocation policy. This protects the rights of both patients and prevents the AI from acting as a judge of human worth.",
      "start_char": 3413,
      "end_char": 3763,
      "token_count": 57,
      "boundary_class": "CONVERGENCE",
      "node_type": "SYN",
      "node_family": "CONVERGENCE",
      "classification_confidence": 1.0
    }
  ],
